WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.720
In 1972, Incoh's 381-meter stack cleared Sudbury's air and sent the sulfur elsewhere. This

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:14.560
is unintended consequences, Episode 154. A chimney built to lift a city's smoke, the

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.700
rules that counted that lift as success, the rain that fell far downwind, and the later

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:25.720
choice to count the sulfur itself. The inco-nickel smelter in Sudbury, Ontario, finished that chimney

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:32.020
in 1972. At the time, it was the tallest in the western hemisphere. Company engineers

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.420
and local officials wanted the sulfur dioxide high enough that the wind would carry it

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.620
past the city. The same emissions came down hundreds of kilometers away as acid rain.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:47.100
To see why the height looked like an answer, you have to stand where they stood. Inside

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.862
a town, the smelters were already hurting. Ground level sulfur dioxide was killing vegetation

00:00:52.862 --> 00:00:58.922
around Sudbury. It was harming residents in the city itself. That was not an abstract regulatory

00:00:58.922 --> 00:01:04.582
puzzle. It was dead ground and people breathing the plume where they lived. The approach then

00:01:04.582 --> 00:01:08.922
current had a slogan that still sounds almost cheerful if you do not know what followed.

00:01:09.562 --> 00:01:15.282
Dilution is the solution to pollution. Height in that framing was a practical way to meet new air

00:01:15.282 --> 00:01:21.002
quality rules without installing expensive scrubbers. Raise the release point, give the gas room,

00:01:21.002 --> 00:01:24.922
let ordinary wind do the mixing the plant was not yet equipped to do.

00:01:25.522 --> 00:01:30.542
In the United States, the 1970 Clean Air Act set national standards that utilities and

00:01:30.542 --> 00:01:34.522
smelters could satisfy by dispersing emissions rather than capturing them.

00:01:35.182 --> 00:01:38.242
The statute did not demand that every ton of sulfur vanish.

00:01:38.802 --> 00:01:42.682
It demanded that the air, as measured against those standards, come into line.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:48.502
Rational actors at the time saw tall stacks as a low-cost bridge while control technology

00:01:48.502 --> 00:01:49.102
improved.

00:01:49.102 --> 00:01:55.602
The bridge metaphor matters. A bridge is not a destination. It is a way to cross until a better road exists.

00:01:56.402 --> 00:02:06.162
Engineers worked the arithmetic that made the bridge look sound. Raising the release point would give the plume more time to mix with larger volumes of air before that plume reached ground level.

00:02:06.862 --> 00:02:14.082
Peak concentrations measured at nearby monitors would fall. If the harm you are trying to stop is a sharp dose right beside the fence.

00:02:14.082 --> 00:02:19.142
That calculation is not a trick. It is physics applied to the problem as defined.

00:02:19.762 --> 00:02:25.082
The regulatory metric was limited to the air people breathed within a few kilometers of the plant fence line.

00:02:25.702 --> 00:02:28.662
Inside that circle, dilution really did lower the reading.

00:02:29.262 --> 00:02:31.842
Outside that circle, the metric had nothing to say.

00:02:32.522 --> 00:02:35.342
Sudbury's officials were not inventing a private loophole.

00:02:35.882 --> 00:02:39.122
They were working inside a shared idea of what compliance meant.

00:02:39.842 --> 00:02:41.562
Protect the people next to the stack.

00:02:41.562 --> 00:02:46.862
Meet the number the monitor can see, spend the money where the rule tells you the money counts.

00:02:47.788 --> 00:02:52.768
Inco finished the Superstack in 1972 at a cost of roughly $25 million.

00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:59.008
Picture that sum as the price of a compliance path, not as a monument for its own sake.

00:02:59.528 --> 00:03:05.628
The company was buying height and with height a way to satisfy the rule without the scrubbers the rule did not yet force.

00:03:05.628 --> 00:03:10.968
course. The idea traveled across the border, the number of stacks taller than 500 feet

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:18.168
rose from 2 in 1970 to more than 180 by 1985, according to the government accountability

00:03:18.168 --> 00:03:25.328
office. 2 than more than 180 in 15 years. That is not a handful of eccentric projects.

00:03:25.848 --> 00:03:30.948
That is an industry learning the same lesson from the same statute. Early measurements showed

00:03:30.948 --> 00:03:37.588
sharp drops in local sulfur dioxide concentrations near both the Sudbury smelter and American power plants.

00:03:38.108 --> 00:03:42.408
Proponents pointed to cleaner air in the immediate vicinity as proof the method worked.

00:03:42.848 --> 00:03:46.688
They had the readings. The readings moved the way the engineers said they would.

00:03:47.128 --> 00:03:50.128
If you lived in Sudbury and the air at street level improved,

00:03:50.588 --> 00:03:54.448
the proof was not a pamphlet. It was the difference in what the city breathed.

00:03:54.848 --> 00:03:57.648
Building the column was not a clean timetable on paper.

00:03:57.648 --> 00:04:01.768
construction crews worked through a labor dispute and even a tornado that

00:04:01.768 --> 00:04:06.628
struck during building. The tapered concrete column stood anyway. It began

00:04:06.628 --> 00:04:10.368
venting gases above the inversion layer that had previously trapped pollution

00:04:10.368 --> 00:04:15.988
over the city. An inversion is a lid. Warmer air sits over cooler air and the smoke

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:20.628
cannot rise through it. For years that lid had held the smelters gases down on

00:04:20.628 --> 00:04:24.888
Sudbury. The superstack was designed to punch through that lid and release the

00:04:24.888 --> 00:04:26.448
plume where the wind could take it.

00:04:27.068 --> 00:04:30.648
Locally, that is exactly what a person hoping to clear a city would want.

00:04:31.328 --> 00:04:36.268
Regulators accepted the height increase because the 1970 statute treated dispersion as an

00:04:36.268 --> 00:04:41.268
acceptable compliance path when add-on controls were judged economically unreasonable.

00:04:42.228 --> 00:04:45.168
Economically unreasonable is a phrase with a human edge.

00:04:45.648 --> 00:04:50.048
It means someone weighed scrubbers against the cost, against the technology, then available,

00:04:50.528 --> 00:04:52.848
and decided the statute allowed another route.

00:04:52.848 --> 00:04:57.528
Height was that route. The government accountability office would later describe

00:04:57.528 --> 00:05:03.328
how widely American plants took it. Sudbury took it in one extraordinary structure. The

00:05:03.328 --> 00:05:08.588
early local gains were real. Cleaner air beside the plants was not a public relations invention.

00:05:09.368 --> 00:05:14.108
Monitors recorded it. What the monitors beside the plants could not record was the fate of

00:05:14.108 --> 00:05:18.863
the gas after it left their range. The emissions themselves did not disappear.

00:05:18.863 --> 00:05:24.283
Here, sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides released high into the atmosphere traveled farther.

00:05:24.703 --> 00:05:28.163
They reacted with moisture to form sulfuric and nitric acid.

00:05:28.763 --> 00:05:31.083
That acid fell as rain far from the source.

00:05:31.783 --> 00:05:37.103
This is the causal chain, and it is worth walking slowly, because nothing in it requires a villain.

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:39.383
The stack did what it was built to do.

00:05:39.943 --> 00:05:41.163
It kept the plume aloft.

00:05:41.703 --> 00:05:43.203
A loft, the plume had time.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.363
Time and moving air is distance.

00:05:45.363 --> 00:05:49.843
distance, distance carried the sulfur out of Sudbury's few kilometers and into weather

00:05:49.843 --> 00:05:53.343
systems that did not stop at a city line or a national border.

00:05:53.883 --> 00:05:56.823
In Sudbury, the landscape had already been stripped bare.

00:05:57.383 --> 00:05:59.623
The Superstack did not create that bareness.

00:06:00.203 --> 00:06:01.963
The smelting that came before it had.

00:06:02.623 --> 00:06:07.823
What the Superstack did was move the same load, north and east, into other Ontario districts,

00:06:08.383 --> 00:06:11.343
across the border into New England and the Adirondacks.

00:06:11.803 --> 00:06:13.523
Same sulfur, different ground.

00:06:13.523 --> 00:06:17.703
found, people in forests that had not stood at the fence line when the permit was written.

00:06:18.243 --> 00:06:23.443
By the mid-1980s, American officials were naming INCO as North America's single largest

00:06:23.443 --> 00:06:24.763
sulfur dioxide emitter.

00:06:25.343 --> 00:06:29.743
A structure built to solve a local air problem had become, in another country's accounting,

00:06:30.383 --> 00:06:32.483
the continent's biggest single source of the gas.

00:06:33.223 --> 00:06:34.843
The acid-load damaged forests.

00:06:35.463 --> 00:06:40.303
It has citified lakes, its strained diplomatic relations between Canada and the United States.

00:06:40.963 --> 00:06:42.743
Diplomacy here is not a side note.

00:06:42.743 --> 00:06:45.663
it is a third-order effect of a measurement choice.

00:06:46.283 --> 00:06:51.043
A permit written against nearby monitors became a cross-border argument about who had sent

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.663
what onto whose watersheds.

00:06:53.203 --> 00:06:57.663
The government accountability office later noted that stack height was only one variable

00:06:57.663 --> 00:06:59.783
among wind patterns and emission volumes.

00:07:00.463 --> 00:07:03.203
The policy had treated height as the decisive control.

00:07:03.803 --> 00:07:08.843
That gap between a complicated sky and a single lever is where the unintended consequence lives.

00:07:09.543 --> 00:07:11.363
Wind patterns were always going to matter.

00:07:11.363 --> 00:07:15.923
Emission volumes were always going to matter. A rule that could be satisfied

00:07:15.923 --> 00:07:20.603
by height alone did not have to wait for those other variables to be managed. Because

00:07:20.603 --> 00:07:26.043
the plume stayed aloft longer, oxidation had more time to occur. A larger fraction of the

00:07:26.043 --> 00:07:31.163
sulfur converted into acidic compounds before deposition. The extra time that was supposed

00:07:31.163 --> 00:07:36.203
to dilute the dose became extra time to change the chemistry. Dilution and transformation

00:07:36.203 --> 00:07:40.783
were happening in the same air. The rule had been written for the first and not for the

00:07:40.783 --> 00:07:46.163
second. Lakes whose watersheds had thin soils and little natural buffering capacity saw

00:07:46.163 --> 00:07:52.363
pH drops that eliminated fish populations. Buffering capacity is the land's ability to neutralize

00:07:52.363 --> 00:07:58.523
acid before the water goes sour. Where soils were thin, that ability was small. Rain that might

00:07:58.523 --> 00:08:03.723
have been absorbed elsewhere landed as a lasting change in the lake. Fish populations disappeared

00:08:03.723 --> 00:08:09.083
from waters that ground-level monitors in Sudbury never sampled. Those monitors were doing their

00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:14.223
assigned job. Their assigned job was the air near the plant. An effect that arrived as

00:08:14.223 --> 00:08:19.543
rain after a chemical change in another watershed was outside the instrument and outside the

00:08:19.543 --> 00:08:24.503
permit. The same windfields that cleared the city also delivered the transformed pollutants

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:29.443
to jurisdictions that had no say in the original stack height permits. That is the political

00:08:29.443 --> 00:08:34.483
shape of the science. The wind that residents of Sudbury could be grateful for was the delivery

00:08:34.483 --> 00:08:37.243
system for communities that never voted on the stack.

00:08:37.763 --> 00:08:41.763
No one in those downwind districts had been asked whether dispersion was an acceptable

00:08:41.763 --> 00:08:44.163
price for Sudbury's cleaner street-level air.

00:08:44.783 --> 00:08:50.603
They received the acid anyway, forest damaged, lakes acidified, fish gone where the soils

00:08:50.603 --> 00:08:55.343
could not buffer the load, and a diplomatic strain between two countries that shared the

00:08:55.343 --> 00:08:58.163
weather and did not share the original compliance decision.

00:08:58.903 --> 00:09:01.483
Hold the empathy and the damage in the same hand.

00:09:01.483 --> 00:09:06.463
The people who approved the height were answering a real injury in Sudbury, with a tool

00:09:06.463 --> 00:09:10.263
the law then blessed, aimed at a metric the monitors could confirm.

00:09:10.923 --> 00:09:13.683
The injury they did not see was not hidden by malice.

00:09:14.223 --> 00:09:16.103
It was hidden by the boundary of the measurement.

00:09:17.167 --> 00:09:22.867
Congress amended the Clean Air Act in 1977 to bar the use of stack heights above good engineering

00:09:22.867 --> 00:09:24.847
practice when demonstrating compliance.

00:09:25.527 --> 00:09:28.307
The amendment did not ban tall chimneys as objects.

00:09:28.307 --> 00:09:33.007
It stopped letting extra height stand in for control when a company showed it had met

00:09:33.007 --> 00:09:33.647
the standard.

00:09:34.187 --> 00:09:36.287
Good engineering practice became the line.

00:09:36.847 --> 00:09:39.267
Above that line, height could no longer be the proof.

00:09:39.827 --> 00:09:43.827
In 1985, Ontario launched its Countdown Acid Rain program.

00:09:44.287 --> 00:09:48.947
The program required INCO and three other major sources to cut provincial sulfur dioxide

00:09:48.947 --> 00:09:51.927
emissions more than 60% by 1994.

00:09:52.767 --> 00:09:54.187
More than 60%.

00:09:54.187 --> 00:09:55.407
Not relocated.

00:09:55.707 --> 00:09:55.887
Cut.

00:09:55.887 --> 00:10:01.547
The deadline sat nine years out, which is the pace of a real industrial turn, not a speech.

00:10:02.207 --> 00:10:08.607
Inco invested in process changes and new, shorter stacks under its clean atmospheric emissions reduction project.

00:10:09.187 --> 00:10:13.507
The logic had flipped, shorter stacks were no longer a failure of dispersion.

00:10:14.007 --> 00:10:17.187
They were part of a system that was supposed to emit less in the first place.

00:10:17.867 --> 00:10:21.047
The Superstack was taken out of regular service in 2020.

00:10:21.047 --> 00:10:26.827
It is now being dismantled, a structure that had defined the skyline as the answer to Sudbury's

00:10:26.827 --> 00:10:32.567
air was coming down because the answer had changed. Sudbury's separate re-greening effort began in

00:10:32.567 --> 00:10:39.407
1978, limestone applications and tree planting. That work has restored millions of trees and earned

00:10:39.407 --> 00:10:45.587
a United Nations award. Millions of trees on ground that smelting had stripped is a recovery you can

00:10:45.587 --> 00:10:51.367
walk through. The award recognizes that recovery. The original tall stack decision had already

00:10:51.367 --> 00:10:56.847
exported part of the damage. Regreening Sudbury did not unexport what the plume had carried

00:10:56.847 --> 00:11:03.267
north, east, and across the border. Both things are true, and they do not cancel. The city could

00:11:03.267 --> 00:11:07.607
heal in place while other districts were still living with the rain the tall release had helped

00:11:07.607 --> 00:11:14.187
deliver. The new stacks and the process modifications cut total sulfur output rather than merely relocating

00:11:14.187 --> 00:11:18.947
it. That is the redesign that matches the original intention more closely than height

00:11:18.947 --> 00:11:24.647
ever could. The intention had been less harm from sulfur. Dispersion had delivered less

00:11:24.647 --> 00:11:30.887
harm in one place. Removal delivered less sulfur in the system. The earlier export of acidity

00:11:30.887 --> 00:11:37.507
had already required decades of liming and replanting on both sides of the border. Decades. Limestone

00:11:37.507 --> 00:11:42.827
on land, trees put back, work that outlasted the era when height counted as compliance.

00:11:42.827 --> 00:11:48.347
stance. The fix, when it came, did not arrive as a single switch. It arrived as amended

00:11:48.347 --> 00:11:54.707
law, a provincial countdown, process changes, shorter stacks, and a long repair of soils

00:11:54.707 --> 00:12:00.287
and forests that the plume had already touched. Dismantling the super stack itself now requires

00:12:00.287 --> 00:12:05.907
careful sequencing so that standby capacity remains available during the transition. Even

00:12:05.907 --> 00:12:10.667
the ending is an engineering problem. You do not simply erase the chimney that once carried

00:12:10.667 --> 00:12:15.667
the compliance case. You take it down in an order that keeps the smelter able to operate

00:12:15.667 --> 00:12:20.867
while the new arrangement holds. The meta-irony is quiet. The stack that was the solution

00:12:20.867 --> 00:12:25.507
became a structure that had to be retired without leaving the plant unable to manage its remaining

00:12:25.507 --> 00:12:31.127
emissions. Hyde had been the whole strategy. In the end, Hyde was the thing that had to be removed

00:12:31.127 --> 00:12:36.569
carefully so that actual reductions could stand on their own. When regulators counted only

00:12:36.569 --> 00:12:41.829
nearby ground-level readings, inco- and American utilities were rewarded for building higher

00:12:41.829 --> 00:12:47.369
rather than for removing sulfur. The reward was compliance. The behavior was concrete,

00:12:47.749 --> 00:12:53.089
steel, and a plume released above the lid of the city. When the metric later expanded to include

00:12:53.089 --> 00:12:58.669
total emissions and downwind deposition, the same companies faced binding reduction targets instead.

00:12:59.269 --> 00:13:05.389
Same firms, same gas, a different boundary around what counted. The shift shows how the choice of

00:13:05.389 --> 00:13:08.749
measurement boundary can turn a local fix into a regional problem.

00:13:09.349 --> 00:13:12.689
If you only score the air inside a few kilometers, height wins.

00:13:13.309 --> 00:13:17.429
If you score the sulfur that leaves the plant and the acid that lands where the wind takes

00:13:17.429 --> 00:13:19.469
it, height stops being the prize.

00:13:20.109 --> 00:13:23.809
That is not a moral upgrade discovered by wiser people looking backward.

00:13:24.309 --> 00:13:26.629
It is a change in what the rule was willing to see.

00:13:27.029 --> 00:13:32.129
Anyone writing a rule today inherits the same temptation the 1970 statute carried.

00:13:32.129 --> 00:13:32.249
Trade.

00:13:32.469 --> 00:13:37.449
Draw the boundary where the instruments are easy, where the politics are local, where

00:13:37.449 --> 00:13:39.069
the improvement shows up fast.

00:13:39.689 --> 00:13:44.069
The improvement can be genuine inside that line and still be a transfer outside it.

00:13:44.689 --> 00:13:50.249
Carbon rules and air quality rules are drawing those lines now, around cities, around facilities,

00:13:50.829 --> 00:13:52.609
around the year a target is checked.

00:13:53.089 --> 00:13:58.009
Environmental intelligence follows how those boundaries get written and revised, which is

00:13:58.009 --> 00:14:01.109
the live version of the argument this chimney settled the hard way.

00:14:01.109 --> 00:14:06.329
Watch the instrument, not the slogan. If the instrument cannot see past the fence,

00:14:06.729 --> 00:14:11.749
the rational project will optimize for the fence. What boundary are today's air quality

00:14:11.749 --> 00:14:16.869
or carbon rules still drawing too narrowly? That's unintended consequences for today.

